{"h": {"measure": "A", "k": 100, "noise": "N2"}, "sp": "nb", "rep": 138, "hyps": [{"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "skip_connect", "cond_edge": 4, "cond_op": "skip_connect", "direction": "lower", "why": "Adding a direct skip to a cell already dominated by skip paths yields a parameter-poor network and hurts accuracy (exp 25, 60)."}, {"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "Placing a conv on an empty direct input-output edge adds a new learnable path rather than replacing an existing one."}, {"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 4, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "With edge 4 absent, removing edge 3 leaves the output reliant on the edge-5 path alone and can disconnect it, collapsing accuracy."}, {"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "When the direct input-output edge is missing, edge 5 is one of few routes to the output, so removing it is far more damaging."}, {"edit_edge": 0, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "Without the direct edge 3, node 1 may carry all information to the output, so cutting edge 0 can disconnect the cell."}, {"edit_edge": 2, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 2, "cond_op": "nor_conv_1x1", "direction": "lower", "why": "Swapping a 1x1 conv for a 3x3 conv brings a much smaller gain than introducing the first conv on edge 2."}, {"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "skip_connect", "cond_edge": 0, "cond_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "direction": "higher", "why": "Conv-heavy cells benefit from a residual shortcut, while parameter-free cells are harmed by more skips."}, {"edit_edge": 0, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 0, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "Activating node 1 with a conv adds capacity, while replacing an identity skip on edge 0 loses a useful shortcut."}, {"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "avg_pool_3x3", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "nor_c